# Goodreads Dataset Setup

## 1. Download Datasets

Download the following datasets from the [UCSD Goodreads Book Graph](https://cseweb.ucsd.edu/~jmcauley/datasets/goodreads.html).

### Required

- [User–Book Interactions (~4.1 GB)](https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads/goodreads_interactions.csv) — Complete dataset of ~228 million interactions, including ratings and reading status.
- [Book Metadata (~2 GB)](https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads/goodreads_books.json.gz) — Metadata for ~2.36 million books.
- [Book ID Mapping](https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads/book_id_map.csv) — Maps interaction book IDs to Goodreads book IDs.

### Additional Metadata

- [Book Works](https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads/goodreads_book_works.json.gz) — Groups different editions of the same literary work.
- [Book Genres](https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads/goodreads_book_genres_initial.json.gz) — Genre classifications for books.
- [Book Series](https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads/goodreads_book_series.json.gz) — Information about book series.
- [User ID Mapping](https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads/user_id_map.csv) — Maps numeric user IDs to the dataset's anonymized Goodreads user IDs.

## 2. Directory Structure

Place all downloaded files in `data/`. Keep `.json.gz` files compressed.

```text
goodreadsmba/
├── data/
│   ├── README.md
│   ├── goodreads_interactions.csv
│   ├── book_id_map.csv
│   ├── user_id_map.csv
│   ├── goodreads_books.json.gz
│   ├── goodreads_book_works.json.gz
│   ├── goodreads_book_genres_initial.json.gz
│   └── goodreads_book_series.json.gz
└── .gitignore
```

## 3. Download via Terminal

Run these commands from the repository root.

### macOS / Linux (Bash)

```bash
mkdir -p data
BASE="https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads"

curl -fL -C - "$BASE/goodreads_interactions.csv" -o data/goodreads_interactions.csv
curl -fL -C - "$BASE/book_id_map.csv" -o data/book_id_map.csv
curl -fL -C - "$BASE/user_id_map.csv" -o data/user_id_map.csv
curl -fL -C - "$BASE/goodreads_books.json.gz" -o data/goodreads_books.json.gz
curl -fL -C - "$BASE/goodreads_book_works.json.gz" -o data/goodreads_book_works.json.gz
curl -fL -C - "$BASE/goodreads_book_genres_initial.json.gz" -o data/goodreads_book_genres_initial.json.gz
curl -fL -C - "$BASE/goodreads_book_series.json.gz" -o data/goodreads_book_series.json.gz
```

### Windows (PowerShell)

```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path data | Out-Null

$base = "https://mcauleylab.ucsd.edu/public_datasets/gdrive/goodreads"

$files = @(
    "goodreads_interactions.csv",
    "book_id_map.csv",
    "user_id_map.csv",
    "goodreads_books.json.gz",
    "goodreads_book_works.json.gz",
    "goodreads_book_genres_initial.json.gz",
    "goodreads_book_series.json.gz"
)

foreach ($file in $files) {
    Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "$base/$file" -OutFile "data/$file"
}
```

**Note:** The complete dataset is several gigabytes. Downloads may take some time depending on your connection.

## 4. Git Configuration

Add the following to the root `.gitignore`:

```gitignore
# Goodreads raw datasets
data/*.json.gz
data/*.csv

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/

The original datasets are provided for academic use and should not be redistributed through the repository.